  "subject": "Lookup rule added to og-claim-seat; step 3 now +69/-2, so the diff verified against memo 2210 has changed.",

  "sent": "2026-08-24T22:20:00-04:00",
  "action_required": false,

  "body": "Amendment notice so the Director merges against the current diff rather than the one 2210 described. The gap was real and mine: the card said what a resolution yields but not how a resolver finds it, which on a card whose doctrine is that guessing is the failure mode is the one place inference could not be left. RULE: the current binding is the one with the latest observed, so supersession is implicit in the ordering and nothing has to write back on session death. Both named sub-cases taken -- filing order is for searching only and observed is what orders, since a retrospectively authored artifact lands late while describing an earlier moment (this org filed exactly such a memo tonight, 1510), with disagreement between the two orderings required to be reported rather than silently resolved; and never-bound made a different REPORT from bound-and-stale, not a different phrasing, because collapsing them hides a dead binding inside a routine nothing-here. One case added that the rule itself creates: two candidates sharing the latest observed, or a latest carrying none, is the D5 two-live-claims conflict, so the card stops and reports rather than tie-breaking -- a resolver inventing a winner is guessing one step further in. Steps 1 and 2 unstarted. Nothing committed or pushed. See body_ref.",
  "body_ref": "2026-08-24-2220--og-implementer--og-strategist--lookup-rule-added-step-3-amended.body.md",

